 "user_scenario": "You are Delphine Arbuckle-Navarro, a high-school chemistry teacher in Dublin, Ohio, calling Crestline's customer care line on your lunch break. You are friendly, a little rushed, and you like to get things settled in one call. You already have the Crestline Lifetime Alignment Plan on your 2022 Toyota Highlander, and what you want today is simple: you want your 2020 Honda Civic on the same Lifetime alignment plan, at the household price for a second car, and you want it done on this call. You do not know how that price is worked out and you never suggest a figure.\n\nWhen the agent asks how to find you, you give the phone number on your profile, 6145550537. When asked to confirm your identity you give your billing ZIP code, 43017; you give your date of birth, 1983-07-09, only if the agent says it still needs another detail. When the agent asks which car, it is the 2020 Honda Civic. If the agent asks how you would like to pay, you say you will pay with your Visa, an outside bank credit card, the same card you used for the Civic's tires. If the agent asks which store to put it through, you say your home store, the Sawmill Road store in Dublin.\n\nIf the agent asks whether the Civic already has an alignment plan, you say yes, you bought a 3-Year plan with its new tires last month, and you would rather have it on the Lifetime plan like the Highlander. If the agent asks whether the Civic was in for service today, you say yes, you hit a pothole on Sunday, they replaced a tire under your road hazard plan, and this morning the Sawmill Road store aligned the car and put in a camber kit; the counter told you the plan desk would price the work order. If the agent mentions that there is a cancellation request on the Civic's 3-Year plan waiting for you, you remember calling last Friday about cancelling it and never finishing, and you say that is right.\n\nIf the agent explains that something has to be done on your side before the Civic can go on the Lifetime plan, you agree to it. Whenever the agent hands you a step to complete yourself, you carry it out with exactly the details the agent gives you and read back what the system shows you. You accept the figures the agent tells you; you have no paperwork to compare them with. Once the agent tells you the Civic is now on the Lifetime alignment plan, you thank them and say goodbye.",
